    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Assistant-Professor_R0013051": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Assistant Professor Job Summary: The School of Nursing and Health Professions at the University of San Francisco invites nominations and applications for a tenure-track faculty position specializing in Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing for prelicensure/post licensure nursing programs at the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of San Francisco. Full Job Description: Successful candidates will be expected to engage in didactic and clinical teaching, scholarship, and service that will contribute to the university and profession. They will develop and teach courses in the area(s) of Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing, be responsible for producing scholarship commensurate with the requirements of tenure, and contribute to the advancement of the School of Nursing and Health Professions through student advisement, service on committees and participation in the broader university and disciplinary communities.   Minimum Qualifications:  o   An earned doctoral degree in nursing or related area and a BSN or MSN if doctoral degree is not in nursing.  o   Upon hire, the faculty member must be licensed as a registered nurse in California.  o   One year of full-time direct patient care experience in Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing within the last 5 years. o   A record of accomplishments in teaching, scholarship and services appropriate for appointment at the rank of a tenure track assistant professor or associate professor. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university standards, including any prior service in a tenure-earning position, and consistent with the university collective bargaining agreement o   A strong commitment to teaching and scholarship, experience and willingness to work in a culturally diverse environment and an understanding of and commitment to support the mission of the University.   We invite candidates to learn more about the program located in the heart of San Francisco https://www.usfca.edu/nursing.   Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $113,633.96 annualized"
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Teaching-Professor--Neuroscience--University-of-San-Francisco_R0013075": {
      "title": "Teaching Professor, Neuroscience, University of San Francisco",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-03\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Teaching Professor, Neuroscience, University of San Francisco Job Summary: The Neuroscience Program at the University of San Francisco invites applications for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor position to begin Fall 2027. Full Job Description: Job Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach neuroscience major courses, serve as a faculty advisor to students in the program, and contribute to other initiatives in service to the department and to the university. The standard teaching load for this position at USF is 24 units per year. Many, but not all, courses are 4 units, so this would amount to a 3-3 teaching load across the academic year. The successful candidate will be able to teach one or more of the program’s distinctively social justice-oriented courses: Neuroscience and the Common Good (a Community-Engaged Learning course), and Neurodiversity, Equity, and Ethics (using a science-and-society lens). They will also teach some subset of the following 4-unit courses: Introduction to Neuroscience (lecture and/or lab), Research Methods & Data Analysis in Neuroscience, and Advanced Research Topics in Neuroscience (a senior capstone course). Additionally, the neuroscience major includes two 1-unit support courses, Preparing for NeuroSuccess and Planning for NeuroCareers, that may constitute part of the candidate’s teaching load as capacity allows. The ideal candidate will also teach and/or contribute to the development of one or more new courses aligned with their specific area of expertise.  Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must possess a PhD in Neuroscience, Biology, Psychology, Cognitive Science, or a related field. ABD candidates will be considered if the degree will be conferred no later than August 2027. This position requires a commitment to excellence in teaching within a culturally diverse environment. A strong record of teaching at the university level and an understanding of and commitment to support the mission of the University of San Francisco are required. Applicants should submit: a cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and experience (which should include reflection on teaching in a culturally diverse educational environment), evidence of teaching ability (e.g., sample syllabi, teaching evaluations), and three letters of recommendation (requested upon submission of application). Additional materials may be requested later in the process. Questions can be addressed to NeuroscienceSearch@usfca.edu . For full consideration, applications should be submitted by the priority deadline of January 5, 2027. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before January 31, 2027 may still be considered.  We invite candidates to find out more about the Neuroscience program at https://www.usfca.edu/arts-sciences/programs/undergraduate/neuroscience. All new faculty have support from the Center for Teaching Excellence and the Center for Research, Artistic and Scholarly Excellence . Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $103,184.83 - $113,633.96 annualized; commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Teaching-Professor--Department-of-Chemistry--University-of-San-Francisco_R0012773": {
      "title": "Teaching Professor, Department of Chemistry, University of San Francisco",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Teaching Professor, Department of Chemistry, University of San Francisco Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry at the University of San Francisco invites applications for a one-year full-time Teaching Professor position at the Assistant Professor level, to begin August 2027. This is a teaching-focused position with no research responsibilities. Our ACS-certified department offers a BS in Chemistry, a BS with Biochemistry concentration, a BS with Medicinal/Synthetic Chemistry concentration, and a thesis-based MS in Chemistry. The department is supported by a full-time stockroom manager, organic lab coordinator/NMR manager, instrumentation specialists, and a science safety officer. Full Job Description: Job Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach General Chemistry and Organic Chemistry lecture and laboratory courses, and may also be asked to teach Medicinal Chemistry. A full-time teaching assignment consists of a combination of lecture sections (4 units each) and laboratory sections (2 units each) totaling 12 teaching units per semester. The successful candidate will also be expected to engage in service to the d epartment and college.   Minimum Qualifications : Applicants should hold a Ph.D. (or expect to complete their Ph.D. by August 202 7 ) in Chemistry or a closely related field. This position requires a commitment to excellence in teaching within a culturally diverse environment. In addition, a strong record of teaching at the university level, evidence of scholarship, and an understanding of and commitment to supporting the mission of the University of San Francisco are required. Applicants should submit: a cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, evidence of teaching ability (e.g., sample syllabi, student and/or peer teaching evaluations), and three letters of recommendation (requested upon submission of application) . Questions can be address ed to chemistrysearch@usfca.edu . Priority will be given to applications received by October 1 , 202 6 .   We invite candidates to find out more about the Department of Chemistry at https://www.usfca.edu/arts-sciences/programs/undergraduate/chemistry/program-overview . In addition all new faculty have access to support from the Center for Teaching Excellence and the Center for Research, Artistic and Scholarly Excellence . Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $103,184.83 - $113,633.96 annualized; commensurate with experience"
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Visiting-Assistant-Professor--Teaching-Appointment--Environmental-Science--University-of-San-Francisco_R0012494": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Teaching Appointment, Environmental Science, University of San Francisco",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-22\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Visiting Assistant Professor, Teaching Appointment, Environmental Science, University of San Francisco Job Summary: The Department of Environmental Science at the University of San Francisco invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor position for the 2027 calendar year to begin January 2027, with the possibility of renewal contingent upon funding approval. Candidates with interdisciplinary training in ecology and/or water resources are preferred, but other areas of specialization within the sphere of environmental science and management will be considered. The successful candidate will have breadth in environmental science and management and will contribute to both the Master of Science in Environmental Management (MSEM) and the Bachelor of Science in Environmental Science (ENVS) degrees offered by the Environmental Science Department. Full Job Description: Job Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in environmental science and management, including introductory, capstone, and elective courses, depending on their area of expertise. The teaching load for this position is 24 units for the year, split between the graduate and undergraduate programs. This teaching load includes a combination of semester-long undergraduate courses (4 units) and half-semester graduate courses (2 units). Research mentorship responsibilities will include providing individualized support in the development and realization of graduate capstone projects. In addition, the successful candidate will be expected to engage in service to the Department and College. Minimum Qualifications : A PhD or appropriate terminal degree in their field with the expertise to teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in two or more of the following areas: introductory environmental science, environmental chemistry, environmental statistics and/or geospatial science (GIS), natural resources/water resources management, ecosystem science, ecological restoration,  as well as broader management courses including but not limited to environmental remediation, risk assessment and management, climate change mitigation and urban sustainability/resilience. Experience advising students in independent research is required so that the candidate can support courses such as Research Methods and the Master's Project in our graduate program. This position requires a commitment to excellence in teaching within a culturally diverse environment. A strong record of teaching at the university level and an understanding of and commitment to the University of San Francisco's mission are required. Applicants should submit: 1) a cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications; 2)  a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, which should include what courses the candidate is interested in teaching and a reflection on teaching in a culturally diverse educational environment; 4) evidence of teaching ability (e.g., sample syllabi, teaching evaluations); and 5) three letters of recommendation, requested upon submission of application. Additional materials may be requested later in the process. Questions can be addressed to envs.search@usfca.edu . For full consideration, applications should be submitted by July 15, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.  We invite candidates to find out more about the ENVS and MSEM programs at the ENVS website , the MSEM website , and the MSEM Blog . In addition, all new faculty have access to a free membership with the National Center for Faculty Development and Diversity and support from the Center for Teaching Excellence and the Center for Research, Artistic and Scholarly Excellence . Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $103,184.83-$113,633.96 annualized; commensurate with experience"
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Assistant-Professor_R0011797": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-03\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Assistant Professor Job Summary: The School of Nursing and Health Professions at the University of San Francisco invites nominations and applications for term faculty positions in the Psychiatric Mental Health (PMH) Nurse Practitioner and Family Nurse Practitioner Doctor of Nursing Practice and post-graduate PMHNP and/or FNP certificate programs at the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of San Francisco: Full Job Description: Successful candidates will be expected to engage in didactic and clinical teaching, scholarship, and service that will contribute to the university and profession. They will develop and teach courses in the area of PMH and family practice advanced practice nursing, be responsible for producing scholarship commensurate with the requirements of tenure, and contribute to the advancement of the School of Nursing and Health Professions through student advisement, service on committees and participation in the broader university and disciplinary communities.   Minimum Qualifications:  An earned doctoral degree in nursing or related area and a BSN or MSN if doctoral degree is not in nursing.  Upon hire, the faculty member must be licensed as a registered nurse and possess an NP certificate in appropriate area, PMHNP and/or FNP in California .  Three years of full-time direct patient care experience as PMHNP and/or FNP within the last 5 years. A record of accomplishments in teaching, scholarship and services appropriate for appointment at the rank of a term assistant professor or associate professor. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university standards, including any prior service in a tenure-earning position, and consistent with the university collective bargaining agreement A strong commitment to teaching and scholarship, experience and willingness to work in a culturally diverse environment and an understanding of and commitment to support the mission of the University. We invite candidates to learn more about the program located in the heart of San Francisco https://www.usfca.edu/nursing. Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : Assistant Professor Step 5 - $103,184.83 annualized"
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/USF_Full-Time_Faculty/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Jesuit-Chair-in-Catholic-Social-Thought_R0013056-1": {
      "title": "Jesuit Chair in Catholic Social Thought",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Jesuit Chair in Catholic Social Thought Job Summary: The University of San Francisco invites applications for the Jesuit Chair in Catholic Social Thought. As a distinguished scholar in residence, supported by the Lo Schiavo endowment, the Jesuit Chair has the opportunity to pursue research, teaching, and service activities in his or her area of expertise and to enhance the University of San Francisco’s impact in the area of Catholic Social Thought. In close collaboration with the Director of the Joan and Ralph Lane Center for Catholic Social Thought and the Ignatian Tradition and the Vice President for Mission and Ignatian Imagination, the Jesuit Chair will support faculty, staff, and student engagement with Catholic social thought and the Ignatian tradition through Lane Center programming, guest lectures, workshops, and public events. Full Job Description: Minimum qualifications include a PhD in theology, ethics or a related field. The ideal candidate will bring a record of scholarly work and teaching that engage the Catholic, Ignatian imagination.  Members of the Society of Jesus will be given preference for the position.  The term of appointment is flexible, to be mutually agreed upon by the University and the candidate. The position is open to scholars in all disciplines.  Applicants should submit the following: a letter of application outlining the candidate’s expertise in Catholic Social Thought and the Ignatian Tradition and a curriculum vitae. We will begin to review complete applications on November 5, 2026 and will continue to review applications until the position is filled.   Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $45,000 for the Fall 2027 semester"
    }
